<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Meet five Paderborn engineers exploring how humans and AI can build better software together.">
  <title>Team The Human-in-the-Loop | Agentic SE Lab</title>
  <script>
    (() => {
      try {
        const saved = localStorage.getItem("upb-theme");
        const theme = saved === "light" || saved === "dark"
          ? saved
          : (window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light");
        document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
      } catch (_) {
        document.documentElement.setAttribute(
          "data-theme",
          window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light"
        );
      }
    })();
  </script>
  <style>
    :root {
      --accent: #E4007C;
    }

    [data-theme="light"] {
      --bg: #FFF8E7;
      --text: #1D1D1F;
      --secondary: #5A5A5F;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      --line: #E9E2D5;
      --shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
      --soft: #F8F1E2;
    }

    [data-theme="dark"] {
      --bg: #14142B;
      --text: #F4F1DE;
      --secondary: #B8B5A7;
      --card: #1F1F3D;
      --line: #353555;
      --shadow: none;
      --soft: #252545;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
      transition: background-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    a:focus-visible,
    button:focus-visible {
      outline: 0.2rem solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: 0.2rem;
    }

    .wrap {
      width: min(100% - 3rem, 70rem);
      margin-inline: auto;
    }

    .site-header {
      padding: 2rem 0 2.5rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .header-row {
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    h1,
    h2,
    h3,
    p {
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    h1 {
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    }

    .tagline {
      max-width: 42rem;
      margin-bottom: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    #theme-toggle {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.55rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
      background: var(--card);
      color: var(--text);
      font: inherit;
      cursor: pointer;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    #theme-toggle:hover {
      border-color: var(--accent);
    }

    .toggle-icon {
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      line-height: 1;
    }

    main {
      padding-block: 3rem;
    }

    section + section {
      margin-top: 4rem;
    }

    .section-intro {
      max-width: 48rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
      line-height: 1.2;
      letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    }

    .section-intro p {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .member-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .member-card {
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid transparent;
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .member-photo {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: 14rem;
      object-fit: cover;
      background: var(--soft);
    }

    [data-theme="dark"] .member-photo {
      filter: brightness(0.9);
    }

    .card-content {
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .member-card h3 {
      margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
      line-height: 1.25;
    }

    .study {
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .card-content h4 {
      margin: 1.05rem 0 0.2rem;
      font-size: 0.83rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .card-content p {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .interests {
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .hot-take {
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
      border-left: 0.2rem solid var(--accent);
      padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem;
      background: var(--soft);
      border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
    }

    .hot-take strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .future-panel {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .future-panel p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .future-points {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .future-point {
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: 1rem;
      background: var(--soft);
    }

    .future-point strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    footer {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      padding: 1.4rem 1rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .wrap {
        width: calc(100% - 2rem);
      }

      .site-header {
        padding-block: 1.4rem 1.8rem;
      }

      .header-row {
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: stretch;
        gap: 1.1rem;
      }

      #theme-toggle {
        align-self: flex-start;
      }

      .member-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .member-photo {
        height: 16rem;
      }

      .future-points {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      main {
        padding-block: 2rem;
      }

      section + section {
        margin-top: 3rem;
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      *,
      *::before,
      *::after {
        scroll-behavior: auto !important;
        transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
        animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
        animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="wrap header-row">
      <div>
        <h1>Team The Human-in-the-Loop</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Five engineers, one very patient review queue, and a shared belief that “it compiled” is not the same as “it’s correct.”</p>
      </div>
      <button id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch to night mode">
        <span class="toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">☾</span>
        <span class="toggle-label">Night mode</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="wrap">
    <section id="team" aria-labelledby="team-heading">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="team-heading">Meet the team</h2>
        <p>Signal processing, cloud workflows, embedded wires, and at least one strong anti-anime position: here are the humans steering the agents.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="member-grid">
        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:gagan.jpeg}}" alt="Gagan, team member">
          <div class="card-content">
            <h3>Gagan</h3>
            <p class="study">M.Sc. Electrical Systems Engineering at Paderborn University, specializing in signal and information processing; B.Sc. in Electronics and Communication Engineering.</p>
            <h4>Interests</h4>
            <p class="interests">Bike rides, music, and fitness.</p>
            <h4>Fun fact</h4>
            <p>I hate anime.</p>
            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p>Agents write a lot of code, but still need human supervision to understand requirements and produce well-structured software.</p>
            <h4>In 5–10 years</h4>
            <p>Agents will handle more complex work from fewer prompts. Engineers will increasingly supervise, review, and help teams ship faster with fewer people.</p>
            <div class="hot-take"><strong>Hot take</strong>Developers won't be replaced by AI, but developers who don't supervise it well will be replaced by those who do.</div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:namit.jpg}}" alt="Namit, team member">
          <div class="card-content">
            <h3>Namit</h3>
            <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, 5th semester.</p>
            <h4>Interests</h4>
            <p class="interests">Football, chess, and vibe-coding random projects for fun.</p>
            <h4>Fun fact</h4>
            <p>Left-handed—like roughly one person in ten.</p>
            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p>When AI is great at writing code, engineers add value by deciding what is worth building and how the pieces should fit together.</p>
            <h4>In 5–10 years</h4>
            <p>AI will write most code; engineers will focus more on product decisions and architecture than on programming every line themselves.</p>
            <div class="hot-take"><strong>Hot take</strong>AI is making us lose our edge: we can't even reply to an email anymore without pasting it into ChatGPT first.</div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:ranjith.png}}" alt="Ranjith, team member">
          <div class="card-content">
            <h3>Ranjith</h3>
            <p class="study">M.Sc. Electrical Systems Engineering (Signal &amp; Information Processing) at Universität Paderborn.</p>
            <h4>Interests</h4>
            <p class="interests">Python backends and automation; computer vision on real hardware; reinforcement learning for drone navigation.</p>
            <h4>Fun fact</h4>
            <p>Building a kitchen staff-tracking system using LiDAR instead of cameras—so nobody gets filmed.</p>
            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p>AI speeds up boilerplate, glue code, and getting unstuck, but its confident mistakes make understanding and reviewing every line essential.</p>
            <h4>In 5–10 years</h4>
            <p>Agents will implement more while engineers specify, review, and test. System design, domain knowledge, testing, and observability will matter even more.</p>
            <div class="hot-take"><strong>Hot take</strong>AI won't replace engineers, but it will expose the ones who never understood the code they were copying.</div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:sarpesh.jpg}}" alt="Sarpesh, team member">
          <div class="card-content">
            <h3>Sarpesh</h3>
            <p class="study">M.Sc. Electrical Systems Engineering, 3rd semester, Paderborn University.</p>
            <h4>Interests</h4>
            <p class="interests">Embedded systems, power electronics, automation and control, and engineering with AI tools.</p>
            <h4>Fun fact</h4>
            <p>I spend more time debugging wiring than code, and the wiring usually wins.</p>
            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p>AI agents are useful for boilerplate, scripts, and explaining unfamiliar code—but confident mistakes mean every change needs review and testing.</p>
            <h4>In 5–10 years</h4>
            <p>Engineers will specify and verify more, with domain expertise in areas like embedded systems helping judge whether generated solutions are safe and correct.</p>
            <div class="hot-take"><strong>Hot take</strong>An AI that writes code you can't verify isn't saving time; it's just moving the bug to production faster.</div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:soumya.png}}" alt="Soumya Bani, team member">
          <div class="card-content">
            <h3>Soumya Bani</h3>
            <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science student at Paderborn University, Germany.</p>
            <h4>Interests</h4>
            <p class="interests">DevOps, AI, cloud computing, and enhancing real-world engineering workflows with AI automation.</p>
            <h4>Fun fact</h4>
            <p>Building a multi-agent incident management system to investigate incidents and streamline operations.</p>
            <h4>AI in software engineering today</h4>
            <p>AI boosts productivity, but architecture, debugging, reliability, and security still demand strong engineering fundamentals.</p>
            <h4>In 5–10 years</h4>
            <p>Engineers will orchestrate increasingly autonomous agents that build, test, deploy, and monitor systems, setting constraints and validating results.</p>
            <div class="hot-take"><strong>Hot take</strong>The future belongs to engineers who know what to automate and, more importantly, what not to.</div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="future-of-se" aria-labelledby="future-heading">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="future-heading">The Future of Software Engineering</h2>
        <p>Our shared take: the job is changing, not disappearing. The keyboard may get less exercise; engineering judgment definitely won't.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="future-panel">
        <p>Across our team, AI is already a powerful partner for boilerplate, quick scripts, exploration, and getting unstuck. But generating code is only one small part of making dependable software. Agents can misunderstand requirements, make confident mistakes, or produce code that looks plausible while quietly ignoring the system around it. Humans still need to set direction, understand the domain, design the architecture, and check that the result is correct, secure, reliable, and—where hardware is involved—safe.</p>
        <p>Over the next 5–10 years, we expect more implementation, testing, deployment, and monitoring to be delegated to increasingly capable agents. Engineers will shift toward specifying what should happen, deciding what is worth building, orchestrating tools, and validating outcomes. In other words: fewer hours typing every line, more responsibility for knowing whether those lines deserve to exist.</p>
        <div class="future-points">
          <div class="future-point"><strong>Delegate the typing</strong>Let agents accelerate implementation and repetitive work.</div>
          <div class="future-point"><strong>Keep the judgment</strong>Product thinking, architecture, and domain expertise make output useful.</div>
          <div class="future-point"><strong>Verify the result</strong>Testing, review, observability, reliability, and security are non-negotiable.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>Built by an agent, supervised by humans. 2026 · The Human-in-the-Loop</footer>

  <script>
    (() => {
      const button = document.getElementById("theme-toggle");
      const icon = button.querySelector(".toggle-icon");
      const label = button.querySelector(".toggle-label");

      function updateButton(theme) {
        const switchTo = theme === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
        button.setAttribute("aria-label", `Switch to ${switchTo} mode`);
        icon.textContent = theme === "dark" ? "☀" : "☾";
        label.textContent = theme === "dark" ? "Day mode" : "Night mode";
      }

      updateButton(document.documentElement.getAttribute("data-theme"));

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const nextTheme = document.documentElement.getAttribute("data-theme") === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
        document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", nextTheme);
        try {
          localStorage.setItem("upb-theme", nextTheme);
        } catch (_) {
          // Theme still changes for this visit if storage is unavailable.
        }
        updateButton(nextTheme);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

